### Reviewer 1

The work by Bentley et al. is an excellent step forward in the use of animal movement data to understand how migratory species connect sites across the globe. The work that the authors present is an outstanding task that sets up the scene nicely to better understand how marine ecosystems are inter-connected through large marine vertebrates movement, as well as to better design management strategies across countries and their jurisdictions.
The dataset and the web interface available at MiCO have a huge potential for large-scale efforts and collaborations focused on the interconnectivity of regions of the global ocean.
I commend the authors for their effort and for producing a well-written and robust manuscript. I have added a few comments and questions that I had while reading the paper (see attached PDF), but in general, I think this manuscript should be accepted for publication.
Looking forward to seeing this published

